  "notes": "Cash basis village with governmental and proprietary (Electric, Water, Sewer, Sanitation) funds. Governmental lines from Total column of p4; business-type from Total column of p6. Interest income 7,974 and TIF receipts 64,038 are printed under Other Financing Sources (after Total Receipts) and recorded as receipts with outside_printed_total; TIF categorized as property tax (review). Governmental disbursements are listed by object for the most part (personnel, operating, supplies); Operating expenses and Supplies and materials mapped to streets/highways (Street Fund), Personnel services to general government (mostly General Fund), with review; business-type disbursements by object mapped to utilities. Proprietary Other receipts 4,618 is Electric fund. Cash flow statement (p7-8) is cash basis so proprietary is null. Detail: p9 Budgetary Basis Budget and Actual - All Funds schedule recorded (combines governmental and business-type funds; Charges for services, Interest and Other lines mix both fund types and are flagged; fund_type of those lines is the dominant/first one); transfers in/out recorded as other financing and the printed totals include them. Read pages 1-9 of 9. Detail (user 2026-10-27): per-fund lines from the fund statements' columns (p4, p6) replace the combined schedule. Re-check (attempt 3, user 2026-10-27 balance sheet rule): governmental balance-sheet lines now come from the p3 Statement of Assets and Fund Balances - Cash Basis - Governmental Funds Total column (total 402,012 equals the government-wide governmental column on p1), with fund balance by classification (Restricted -8,691, Unassigned 410,703); proprietary lines and the combined totals stay from the p1 Statement of Net Position (they equal the p5 proprietary statement)."
